From: Olof Johansson <olof@lixom.net>
Subject: [PATCH] arch/riscv/cpu/generic: dram_init via device_type lookup

The bhx daemon's DTB names the memory node with its unit
address (`/memory@400030000000`). Upstream `dram_init` calls
`fdtdec_setup_mem_size_base()` which does an `ofnode_path("/memory")`
literal lookup — that misses unit-addressed nodes. dram_init returns
-EINVAL silently and U-Boot falls back to CFG_SYS_SDRAM_BASE =
0x80000000 (the qemu default), placing the relocated U-Boot image and
its malloc heap at ~0x17e00000_00 instead of inside the actual
0x4000_3000_0000 + 4 GiB L2CPU DRAM range. virtqueue allocations then
land outside DRAM and the host-side virtio worker panics with
"virtqueue desc address X below L2CPU memory start".

Switch to `fdtdec_setup_mem_size_base_lowest()` which walks
device_type="memory" via get_next_memory_node and handles unit-
addressed nodes correctly. dram_init_banksize already uses the
device_type walker so this aligns the two halves.

See bhx #49.

---
--- a/arch/riscv/cpu/generic/dram.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/cpu/generic/dram.c
@@ -12,7 +12,20 @@
 
 int dram_init(void)
 {
-	return fdtdec_setup_mem_size_base();
+	/*
+	 * bhx: use the _lowest variant which walks device_type="memory"
+	 * via get_next_memory_node, so a unit-addressed
+	 * `/memory@400030000000` (our daemon's DTB shape, see #46) is
+	 * found. The original `fdtdec_setup_mem_size_base` calls
+	 * `ofnode_path("/memory")` which only matches the literal node
+	 * name with no unit address; on bhx hardware that fails
+	 * silently and U-Boot falls back to CFG_SYS_SDRAM_BASE =
+	 * 0x80000000 (the qemu default), which makes virtqueue desc
+	 * addresses land outside our actual DRAM range and the daemon
+	 * panics with "addr below L2CPU memory start". See bhx
+	 * #49.
+	 */
+	return fdtdec_setup_mem_size_base_lowest();
 }
 
 int dram_init_banksize(void)
